course: dictionary
lesson: 14936
title: One word, many meanings: registry
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A registry is an official place where records are kept, or an official list of things or people. The clues in a sentence tell you which meaning is right. «The baby's birth was written down in the registry.» Written down and official tell you it is a record, not a cupboard.
explain: Words can change meaning in different countries. In the UK, «We got married at the registry office, with no church service» means a place where people can marry without a church. In the USA, «Aunt Maya added a cot to her baby registry» means a gift list kept at a shop.
explain: Check the meaning by swapping in a word like list or office. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning. «The council keeps a registry of every dog in town» works with list, so registry means an official list here.
fact: A registry is an official place or office where records are kept.
fact: «Registry» can also mean an official list or record, such as a registry of ships.
fact: In the UK, a registry office is where people can get married without a church service.
fact: In the USA, a wedding or baby registry is a gift list kept at a shop.
fact: On a computer, a registry is a store of settings.
exercise: «The baby's birth was written down in the registry.» What is a registry here? | A cupboard for toys | A kind of sweet | * An official record of births | A bus route
exercise: «We got married at the registry office, with no church service.» Which meaning fits? | A shop that sells rings | A school for brides | * A place where people can marry without a church | A park with a lake
exercise: «Aunt Maya added a cot to her baby registry.» What is a baby registry? | * A gift list kept at a shop for a new baby | A type of pram | A ward in a hospital | A list of names from the newspaper
test: «The council keeps a registry of every dog in the town.» What does registry mean? | * An official list or record of things or people | A park for walking dogs | A dog kennel
test: «Changing that setting in the registry fixed the game.» Where are settings kept in this sentence? | In a shop window | * In a store of settings inside a computer | In the school library
exam: Which word fits best? «The ___ kept a record of every ship that sailed from the port.» | Playground | Kitchen | * Registry | Umbrella
